      },
      "message": "fix(drilling): judge a cross drill against the finished part\n\nA cross (radial) drill was never checked against the part it leaves:\non a solid bar with no modelled hole, or past a modelled hole's floor,\nit posted a hole the finished part does not have. The reach, spindle\nand rapid laws judge where the drill stands and travels, not what it\ncuts.\n\nThe cross arm now sweeps the finished chain - the drill's radius along\nthe hole axis from the station to the tip, the point cone, shank and\nholder, posed along each move's tool axis - through the part's solid\n(the verify crate's solid law, the axial verdict's 0.01 mm gouge\ntolerance), and refuses by name: the hole, how deep the tip got, and\nwhether the model has no hole there or the drill runs past its floor.\nThe refusal is a generation error, so nothing reaches the post.\n\nThe cross suites drilled solid bars with no modelled hole; they now\nmodel their holes (tests/punched_bar). The bar is longer (z -80..20,\ntop unchanged) and each hole carries its half-turn image, because the\nlathe axis reader refuses an r10 x 40 bar with a cross hole (#152,\nnot touched here). Decisions in RECOMMENDED.md.\n\nPinned by drilling_cross_part: a_cross_drill_into_a_solid_bar_is_refused_by_name,\na_cross_hole_deeper_than_the_modelled_hole_is_refused,\na_cross_hole_matching_its_modelled_hole_is_clean.\n\nFixes #117\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
